---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About D. Philhower Studio — brand creation and corporate identity for family businesses, informed by Swedish, Japanese, and Art Deco design lineages."
  path="/about"
  headerTheme="dark"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="brand-line">D. Philhower Studio</p>
    <div class="deco-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <h1>A studio for identities that feel inevitable.</h1>
    <p>
      We design custom brand systems and websites for founders, families, and organizations who want their
      presence to match their longevity.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section prose-block reveal" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">The practice</p>
      <div class="deco-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="story-title">Craft over clutter.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>
        D. Philhower Studio specializes in custom brand creation, corporate identity for family businesses,
        and website design. The work is informed by research into Swedish graphic culture — from Olle Eksell’s
        design programs to today’s Stockholm studios — and by Japanese principles of reduction and ma.
      </p>
      <p>
        Art Deco contributes structure: tall type, geometric framing, brass accents. The CBS cafeteria type
        wall contributes energy: language as a physical surface. Together they shape systems that feel both
        permanent and alive.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="values-title">
    <p class="section-label">How we show up</p>
    <div class="deco-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <h2 class="section-title" id="values-title">Principles that shape every engagement.</h2>
    <ul class="values">
      <li>
        <h3>Clarity first</h3>
        <p>Swedish functionalism: if it doesn’t communicate, it doesn’t ship. Hierarchy leads.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Space as structure</h3>
        <p>Japanese ma: what we leave out gives the mark and the message their weight.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Continuity over costume</h3>
        <p>Family identity evolves without abandoning the story that earned trust.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-label="Studio focus">
    <ul class="stat-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Brand + web</strong>
        <span>One language across identity and site — the two surfaces people meet you first.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Family corporate identity</strong>
        <span>Heritage treated as strategy. Systems built for the next generation of stewards.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Researched craft</strong>
        <span>Swedish, Japanese, Deco, and mid-century type lineages — synthesized, not imitated.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-strip reveal" aria-labelledby="about-cta">
    <div class="contact-strip-inner">
      <h2 id="about-cta">Let’s build something with weight.</h2>
      <p>Share a bit about the business and the chapter ahead.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/influences">Explore influences</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
